WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.910
YUFENG GUO: Getting explanations
for your predictions

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:05.250
is becoming
increasingly important.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:08.580
How can we use Cloud AI
Platform's Prediction service

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:10.890
to generate explanations?

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:12.450
Stay tuned to find out.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:15.432
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.110
Welcome to "AI Adventures" where
we explore the art, science,

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:27.270
and tools of machine learning.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:29.400
My name is Yufeng Guo,
and on this episode,

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.910
we're going to explore AI
Explanations, which is now

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:35.310
built into Cloud AI
Platform's Prediction service,

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:38.150
allowing you to have feature
attributions for each

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:40.100
and every one of
your predictions.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.160
AI Explanations integrates
feature attributions

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.410
into AI Platform
Prediction and it

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.540
helps you understand
your model's outputs

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:50.510
for classification
and regression tasks.

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:52.970
This means AI
Explanations can tell you

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.280
how much each
feature in the data

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.080
contributed to the
predicted results.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.350
This is super useful
because you can then

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:03.770
verify the model is behaving
as you would expect, recognize

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:08.030
bias as it's happening, and get
ideas for how you can improve

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:10.360
your training data and model.

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:13.190
Feature attributions are
available for tabular data as

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:15.920
well as image data,
and are specific

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:17.270
to individual predictions.

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:20.750
Currently, there is the
limitation in AI Explanations

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:25.760
that it only supports models
trained on TensorFlow 1.x.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:28.630
And if you're using Keras
to specify your model,

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:31.520
you will need to convert
it into an estimator using

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.050
the model to estimator utility.

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:36.290
Now, let's talk a little
bit about the particulars

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:38.855
of feature attribution
and how it works.

00:01:38.855 --> 00:01:42.020
AI Explanations
offers two methods--

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:45.500
sampled Shapley and
integrated gradients.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:49.730
Both methods are based on the
concept of Shapley values,

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:52.310
which is a cooperative
game theory algorithm that

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:55.160
assigns credit to
each player in a game

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:56.750
for a particular outcome.

00:01:56.750 --> 00:02:01.220
Here, each feature is treated
as a player in that game.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:03.170
And proportional
credit is assigned

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:07.430
to each of those features for
the outcome of a prediction.

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:09.440
Integrated gradients
are best suited

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.290
for differential models
like neural networks.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:15.230
It's especially useful for
models with large feature

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:16.190
spaces.

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:19.490
It computes the gradients
of the output with respect

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:22.220
to the input,
multiplied element-wise

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:24.380
with the input itself.

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:27.150
For those who remember
their calculus class,

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:30.290
this is, essentially, a Taylor
approximation of the prediction

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:32.750
function at the input.

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:34.970
Bet you didn't expect to
see a Taylor approximation

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:36.050
reference today.

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:38.780
Now, let's talk briefly about
the other feature attribution

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:39.380
method--

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:40.940
sampled Shapley.

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:43.460
It assigns credit for the
outcome of each feature

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:46.970
and also considers different
permutations of those features,

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:49.970
and is most suitable for
non-differential models

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:52.040
like ensembles of trees.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:54.470
There are a number of
articles and research papers

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:58.040
which dive way deeper into these
explainability methods which

00:02:58.040 --> 00:02:59.480
I've linked to below.

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:02.910
They're all very well-written
and super interesting to read.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:06.200
So if you like these topics, I
would encourage you to dive in

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.250
and check them out.

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:09.470
If you are ready to
try out AI Explanations

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:11.900
for your deployed model,
head on over to the guides

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:13.280
in the documentation.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:16.400
There's one for tabular data
and another one for image data.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.550
And, best of all, they're
presented as Colab notebooks,

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:21.660
so it's super easy
to try it out.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:23.750
One final note
before we wrap up.

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:26.660
Last episode, we talked
about the What-If Tool,

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:28.730
an open-source tool
for understanding

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:30.510
your model's predictions.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:34.310
AI Explanations can be used in
concert with the What-If Tool

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:36.170
to get an even more
in-depth understanding

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:37.490
of your predictions.

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:40.700
The process for doing that is
also detailed in those Colab

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:42.680
notebooks I mentioned
earlier, and I'll

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:45.060
be sure to link to it in
the description below.

